@startuml
!theme plain
title DB Transactional Outbox + Kafka Consumer Inbox (Synthetic)
autonumber
actor Merchant
participant "Payment API" as API
database "Payments DB" as DB
participant "Outbox Relay / CDC" as Relay
queue "Kafka" as Kafka
participant "Payment State Consumer" as Consumer
participant "Provider Adapter" as Adapter
cloud "External Provider" as Provider
Merchant -> API : POST payment intent + idempotency key
API -> DB : BEGIN; persist intent + attempt + outbox
DB --> API : COMMIT
API --> Merchant : PENDING + intentId
Relay -> DB : Read committed outbox
DB --> Relay : PaymentAttemptCreated(eventId)
Relay -> Kafka : Produce event (stable eventId)
Kafka --> Relay : Broker acknowledgement
Relay -> DB : Mark published / CDC progress

Kafka -> Consumer : Record (may be redelivered)
Consumer -> DB : BEGIN; insert inbox unique key
alt New event and valid state
  Consumer -> DB : Persist guarded state + outbox
else Duplicate or obsolete event
  Consumer -> DB : Record no-op / investigation
end
DB --> Consumer : COMMIT
Consumer -> Kafka : Commit next offset
note over DB,Kafka
Kafka ack and DB commit are not one transaction.
Outbox relay and consumers must tolerate duplicates.
end note
opt Financial command required and not already submitted
  Consumer -> Adapter : Submit with provider-safe semantics
  Adapter -> Provider : Financial instruction with correlation
  Provider --> Adapter : Confirmed response or UNKNOWN
end
@enduml